    old "For a moment, the two newlyweds feverishly kissed one another, forgetting they were not alone."
    new "一瞬、二人の新婚カップルは熱くキス交わし、自分たちが二人きりではないことを忘れていた。"

    old "The priest cleared his throat."
    new "司祭は喉を鳴らした。"

    old "Belmont pulled something from his pocket and held it out to the priest."
    new "ベルモント船長はポケットから何かを取り出し、司祭に差し出した。"

    old "There, holy man. How about you go count these outside for a bit?"
    new "ほら、聖職者さん。外でこれを数えていてくれないか？"

    old "The priest seemed offended at the bribe, but seeing how much coin it was, he quickly changed his mind and left the chapel."
    new "聖職者は賄賂に不快感を示したようだったが、その金額の多さを見て、すぐに考えを変え、礼拝堂を去った。"

    old "Suddenly, they were alone."
    new "突然、二人は二人きりになった。"

    old "What did you do that for?"
    new "何のためにそんなことしたの？"

    old "Well, I was plannin on takin you somewhere fancy, but that was before I saw you in this dress..."
    new "まあ、君をどこか豪華な場所に連れて行くつもりだったんだが、そのドレスを見た後では、そうもいかないだろうな…"

    old "Now I don't think I'd make it to the inn."
    new "今となっては、宿までたどり着けるかどうかだな。"

    old "The alternative was fuckin you out behind a bush somewhere, but I don't feel like that would be a good start to this marriage."
